# Worked examples

## 1. Read-then-act

```json
{
  "name": "comfort check",
  "steps": [
    { "id": "occ", "do": "call", "device": "sensor.occupancy", "action": "read" },
    { "id": "gate", "do": "branch",
      "when": { "gt": ["$.steps.occ.output.count", 0] },
      "then": [
        { "id": "warm", "do": "call", "device": "hvac.zone1",
          "action": "set_target", "with": { "celsius": 22 } }
      ],
      "else": [
        { "id": "eco", "do": "call", "device": "hvac.zone1", "action": "eco_mode" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "output": { "path_taken": "$.steps.gate.output.took" }
}
```

## 2. Parameterized flow with input

```json
{
  "name": "set floor2 brightness",
  "input": { "fields": [ { "name": "level", "type": "number", "required": true } ] },
  "steps": [
    { "id": "east", "do": "call", "device": "light.floor2_east",
      "action": "set_brightness", "with": { "percent": "$.input.level" } },
    { "id": "west", "do": "call", "device": "light.floor2_west",
      "action": "set_brightness", "with": { "percent": "$.input.level" } }
  ]
}
```

## 3. A deployable automation (needs a trigger; run with mode "deploy")

```json
{
  "name": "dock door alert",
  "trigger": { "event": "sensor.door_dock.opened" },
  "steps": [
    { "id": "check", "do": "branch",
      "when": { "gt": ["$.world.time", "21:00"] },
      "then": [
        { "id": "alert", "do": "call", "device": "notify.facilities",
          "action": "send", "with": { "message": "Dock door opened after hours" } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

Comparison note: `gt`/`lt` compare **two numbers** numerically or **two
strings** lexicographically. String comparison on `$.world.time` works
because "HH:MM" is zero-padded, so `{"gt": ["$.world.time", "21:00"]}` is
true after 21:00. Comparing a string to a number is a `type_error` at
validation time.
